      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://dubaiography.com/journal/saudi-arabia-houthi-conflict-yemen-2026",
      "articleSection": "News",
      "url": "https://dubaiography.com/journal/saudi-arabia-houthi-conflict-yemen-2026"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "@id": "https://dubaiography.com/#organization",
      "name": "Dubaiography",
      "url": "https://dubaiography.com"
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is Saudi Arabia at war with Yemen again?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Not in the form of a formally declared war. Saudi Arabia and the Houthis never signed a comprehensive peace deal after their earlier conflict, and the de-escalation that followed a 2022 UN-brokered truce is now breaking down, with Houthi missile and drone attacks on Saudi territory and Saudi-backed operations against Houthi positions in Yemen both intensifying since July 2026." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Why is this escalation different from the earlier Saudi-Houthi war?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "It is happening alongside an active war between the United States and Iran that has largely closed the Strait of Hormuz since February 2026. The Houthis have also seized Yemen's Red Sea coastline and the islands around the Bab al-Mandeb Strait, and a drone strike attributed to Iran-aligned militias in Iraq knocked out Saudi Arabia's main overland oil pipeline, putting pressure on multiple routes at once." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the Bab al-Mandeb Strait and why does it matter?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "It is the narrow waterway between Yemen and the Horn of Africa that ships use to move between the Indian Ocean and the Suez Canal. With the Strait of Hormuz largely closed due to the US-Iran war, Bab al-Mandeb has become one of the Gulf region's remaining major oil and shipping routes, which is why Houthi control over the strait's approaches is significant." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Has the US agreed to strike the Houthis on Saudi Arabia's behalf?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "As of mid-September 2026, no. Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman has reportedly asked President Trump directly for US strikes on Houthi positions, but Washington has so far limited its involvement to intelligence sharing and targeting support rather than direct military action." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What does this mean for the UAE and the wider Gulf?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The UAE faces no direct military threat from the fighting itself, but disruption to either the Strait of Hormuz or Bab al-Mandeb, let alone both at the same time, can raise oil prices, shipping costs and insurance premiums across the Gulf, given how central both routes are to regional trade." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

